# The negative variants of probe-tests/widgets/progress.probe: every test below asserts something WRONG, and every one must FAIL.
# They show that the positive suite can fail, and why. This file does not end in .probe, so `probe test` never picks it up in a directory run. To run it:
#
#   cp probe-tests/negative/progress.probe.expect-fail /tmp/progress-negative.probe
#   probe test /tmp/progress-negative.probe --device <serial> -y       # (the progress build, the same probe.yaml as for progress.probe)
#
# Expected: 0 passed, 3 failed, each with the message in its comment. A test that passes is a finding: either the agent changed or the positive suite no longer proves what it says.

before each test
  restart the app
  wait until #wf_progress_state appears

# Expected: see "Loaded": Expected to see "text("Loaded")" but it was not found (the spinner runs for 3 seconds first)
test "N1 the result straight after the tap"
  tap #wf_load
  see "Loaded"

# Expected: wait until #wf_forever disappears: a timeout after 5 seconds (the spinner never goes away)
test "N2 a spinner that never goes away"
  tap #wf_load_forever
  wait until #wf_forever disappears within 5 seconds

# Expected: see #wf_spinner: Expected to see "#wf_spinner" but it was not found (no spinner before the tap)
test "N3 a spinner before anything was loaded"
  see #wf_spinner
